- Operator precedence: `prev_hash ?? ('"'' + canonicalJson(...))"'` — i.e. when `prev_hash` exists the canonical JSON is *not* included. Obviously unintended, but a literal LLM may implement exactly that. Also schema-engine §2/auth §6 say `sha256(prev_hash ∥ canonical JSON of the row)` — no separator/length-prefix spec; `canonicalJson` key sorting "recursively" — arrays? Unicode? Not specified, and `scripts/verify-audit-chain.mjs` (also T06) must recompute byte-identically from JS — two implementations (TS `audit.ts`, `.mjs` verifier) must agree on JSON canonicalisation with no shared spec.
- **Fix:** write the exact formula in auth-and-tenancy §6: `sha256(utf8( (prev_hash ?? '"'') + '\\n' + canonicalJson(entry) ))"'`, define canonicalJson (sorted keys, no whitespace, arrays in order, numbers via JSON.stringify).

