## C. Prisma schema audit (schema-engine.md §2)

**C1. Relation back-references — one real miss:** `ObjectType.primaryAttributeId` is a bare `String? @db.Uuid` with **no relation** to `Attribute` — intentional? It references attributes.id but has no FK; loading `ObjectTypeDetail.primary_attribute` as a *slug* requires a join the schema can'"'t express. Also "'`RecordChange.relationTypeId`/`linkId` are bare columns without relations to `RelationType`/`RecordLink` — probably intentional (changes survive archives), but undocumented; conversely `ObjectType` is missing a back-relation only if a relation existed. All declared relations *do* have both sides (Attribute.uniqueKeys ↔ RecordUniqueKey.attribute ✔; List.attributes ↔ Attribute.list ✔; Record.linksFrom/linksTo/changes/uniqueKeys/search/listEntries ✔; RelationType.links ✔; PolicyRule.bindings ✔; Team.organization ✔; Organization.teams ✔). **Missing back-relations:** `Record` has no self-relation for `mergedIntoId` (bare column, no FK — acceptable, survivors can be hard-deleted by retention while losers point at them; then redirect breaks — B41'"'s cousin; document intent). Verdict: **MINOR** — add a comment on each intentionally relation-less column ("'`primaryAttributeId`, `mergedIntoId`, `RecordChange.relationTypeId/linkId`, `ApprovalRequest`, `QueueJob`) stating why no FK.

**C2. `Attribute @@unique([objectTypeId, slug])` and `@@unique([listId, slug])` with nullable FKs:** Postgres treats NULLs as distinct → multiple attributes with the same slug and `object_type_id NULL` (pure list attributes) can collide per list? No — `[listId, slug]` covers list attributes; but an attribute with **both** null (neither object type nor list — edge attributes live in `RelationType.edgeAttributes` JSON, so standalone attributes shouldn'"'t exist) — unenforced invariant. Also "'`@@unique([objectTypeId, slug])` is **cross-tenant** — two tenants can'"'t have person.name? No: objectTypeId is per-tenant row, so scoping holds via the parent. ✔ OK. **MINOR:** add a DB check "'`object_type_id IS NOT NULL OR list_id IS NOT NULL` (raw SQL comment absent).

**C3. Enum duplication with auth/contracts — consistent:** Prisma `ActorType` (human/agent/system) matches contracts `ActorType` z.enum ✔; `PolicyScope` matches auth §4 ✔; `PolicyResourceType`/`PolicyAction` match ✔. `PolicyBinding.actorType` is a **plain String** ("human | agent | role") while `ActorType` enum exists — deliberate (role isn'"'t an ActorType) but the comment is the only spec; fine. "'`JobStatus` missing `cancelled` — **B8 (BLOCKER)**.

**C4. `RecordUniqueKey @@unique([attributeId, normalizedValue])` is global across tenants** — correct only if normalized uniqueness is intended per-attribute-per-tenant; attributeId is a tenant-scoped row so uniqueness is effectively per-tenant ✔. But multi-unique: `emails is_multi is_unique` — one key row per array element ✔ (T13 syncUniqueKeys handles). **However** `DUPLICATE_FOUND` read-back "query by `(attribute_id, normalized_value)`" (T13) returns a record from the *same* tenant guaranteed by attribute tenancy ✔. OK.

**C5. Raw-SQL comment/table-name fidelity:** `records_data_gin` on `records(data jsonb_path_ops)` ✔ names match `@@map`. `records_display_name_trgm` ✔. `record_links_active_unique` on `record_links(relation_type_id, from_record_id, to_record_id) WHERE active_until IS NULL` ✔. `record_search` tsv + `record_search_tsv` + `record_search_embedding hnsw vector_cosine_ops` ✔ column names match. **Miss:** T01'"'s lint-migrations guards "'`CREATE INDEX … CONCURRENTLY` on `records|record_changes|record_search` outside the initial migration — but the initial migration'"'s indexes are *not* CONCURRENTLY (impossible in tx) ✔ exempted. **Miss:** §5's runtime "'`attribute.index` job creates indexes named `records_<objtype>_<slug>` on `records` — slug/objtype interpolation into an identifier — the lint only scans migration dirs, not runtime SQL ✔, but identifier length (63 chars) and quoting unspecified — **MINOR**, spec `format('"'%I')"'` or sha-truncation.

**C6. `RecordChange.seq BigInt @default(autoincrement())`** — Prisma autoincrement on non-id BigInt maps to a sequence ✔ Postgres-supported. `Webhook.lastDeliveredSeq BigInt @default(0)` ✔. `IdempotencyReplay @@unique([organizationId, teamId, key])` — `key` unbounded String, fine.

**C7. `datasource extensions = [vector, pg_trgm]`** with `previewFeatures = ["postgresqlExtensions"]` — valid for prisma 6.17 ✔; migration will emit `CREATE EXTENSION IF NOT EXISTS vector` etc. — matches T03'"'s manual appends (duplicates harmless). ✔

**C8. "'`View.filter Json @default("{}")`, `sort @default("[]")`** ✔; `View` has **no relation to ObjectType** (bare `objectTypeId` String) — inconsistent with other models that declare relations; joins for `crm_view_run` (needs object type slug) must query ObjectType separately — works but undocumented. **MINOR**: add relation or comment.

