## D. Turbo/pnpm/script consistency

**D1.** Root `verify` script is defined in T01'"'s package.json ✔ (\""'`pnpm verify` = … (defined in T01)" ✔ true). `prisma:generate` root script filters `@deepcrm/db prisma:generate`; `@deepcrm/db` has extra script `prisma:generate: prisma generate` ✔ names match. **But** `typecheck: pnpm prisma:generate && turbo run typecheck` runs generate on every typecheck — requires schema.prisma (T03+) and a reachable `DATABASE_URL`? `prisma generate` needs no DB ✔, but needs the schema file → A5 stands for T01–T02 acceptance.

**D2.** `turbo.json` task `test` has `dependsOn: ["''^build"]` — vitest runs against `src` via tsx? Package `test: vitest run` with TS source — vitest transpiles itself, no build needed; but `dependsOn: ''^build` forces building deps — fine but slow; `env: ["DATABASE_URL"]` ✔ matches testing.md. `lint dependsOn: ["''^build"]` — eslint on src needs no build; harmless. **MINOR:** persistent `dev` task without `dependsOn` — `pnpm dev` = `pnpm --filter @deepcrm/api dev` (tsx watch) — doesn'"'t generate Prisma client or build deps; first "'`pnpm dev` after install fails on `@prisma/client` import until someone ran `prisma:generate`/`build`. T04 acceptance runs `pnpm dev` after `pnpm typecheck` (which generates) ✔ within-block ordering saves it. OK but fragile — note it.

